{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/prosiform/pulls/622","id":5134545555,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVNSvEM8AAAABMgrykw","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/pull/622","diff_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/pull/622.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/pull/622.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/prosiform/issues/622","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/prosiform/pulls/622/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/prosiform/pulls/622/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/prosiform/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/prosiform/issues/622/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/prosiform/statuses/8ca53994e89dab6657c2eea9eef72f74c48764e0","number":622,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[I10:E04] Composition Following","user":{"login":"m2ux","id":176900785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCotKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176900785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Overview\n\nThe diagram-following eval gains corpus, scorer and harness support for checking how agents follow compiled bundles through composition, deferral and deep dispatch. Scenarios state each agent's ordered `pf` runs, and session traces are checked against those runs and the expected path. The edge-run shakedown, live edge measurements and measured-results documentation are scoped to [I14 Evaluation Refinement](https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/issues/660), in [Composition Measurements](https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/issues/661).\n\n## Changes\n\nThe eval observed only whether a bootstrapping session ran `pf` at all, so no scenario could say which deferred line a session compiles, and no form gave a session a bundle and the build together.\n\n### Stated Runs\n\n- **A scenario states its `pf` runs.**\n  A `[[scenario.compile]]` table names each run's agent and references, in walk order, each held to the sources by the corpus test.\n\n### Compiled Form\n\n- **A compiled session receives a `pf` run's output.**\n  The compiled sources, the entry's bundle set in `pf`'s folder, and the build as `pf` with a shell limited to it.\n\n### Run Checks\n\n- **The scorer holds a session to its stated runs.**\n  `uncompiled`, `overcompiled` and `misordered_compile` follow the dispatch checks wherever a harness reports commands.\n\n### Sub-agent Calls\n\n- **The session record files each call under its sub-agent.**\n  Each start names its parent start and its sub-agent's commands, at the depth each harness declares its stream carries.\n\n### Bootstrap and Deferral\n\n- **A skill's undeclared entry hands over one `↳` line.**\n  `inline-bootstrap` states bare `pf`, then `pf` on the line, and the walk of the bundle it writes; a session that ran no `pf` fails `uncompiled`.\n- **A compiled walk runs `pf` on each `↳` line a step reaches.**\n  `deferred-composition` reaches and passes a conditional and a nested deferral, and `preset-deferral` follows the transition its preset's stand-in states.\n\n### Composition\n\n- **A bundle walk enters a state where a `↳` title or a footnote leads.**\n  `conditional-composition` composes a state beneath a conditional step, entered only where the step holds; `directive-labels` reads a `↳` composition in place, opens a footnote's target as a document, and composes a section of its own document under `W_COMPOSE_SELF`.\n\n### Deferred and Deep Dispatch\n\n- **A deferred section that dispatches is compiled where its step reaches it.**\n  `deferred-dispatch` states `pf` on the `↳` line and the sub-agents its run's bundle dispatches; the dispatch walk records each start's depth.\n- **Chains run three hops below the session.**\n  `dispatch-depth` states a chain, a set at the second hop and a question relayed from the third, with no `W_DISPATCH_DEPTH`.\n- **A sub-agent's `pf` run is stated and shown by its action.**\n  `subagent-first-run` states each sub-agent's run and the files only a deferred line's material names, at the first, second and third hop; one undone fails `missing_action`.\n\n### Claude Compiled Session\n\n- **A compiled Claude session carries a shell.**\n  `Bash`, approved for `pf` alone, reaches the `compiled` and `bootstrap` sessions, so the nested-dispatch scenarios take a Claude cell scored on each start's runs.\n\n### Guide Bundles\n\n- **The corpus test reads the guide's bundles.**\n  Each dispatched bundle carries the run-pf instruction before its source content, each `⇉` link names a file its run wrote, and no source writes a retired mark.\n\n### Triage Rubric\n\n- **The rubric decides each run class.**\n  `uncompiled`, `overcompiled` and `misordered_compile` each take a `miss`, `defect` and `unclear` reading in `RUNBOOK.md`, which holds no row for a class the scorer does not give.\n\n### Harness Observation\n\n- **Admit observed child commands.**\n  `evals/diagram-following/harness.py` declares child starts and per-child commands separately. `evals/diagram-following/run.py` retains native deep chains and excludes scenarios whose child compiler calls cannot be attributed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Complete local and hosted checks pass at `8ca53994e89dab6657c2eea9eef72f74c48764e0`:1,731 source tests,1,586 harness/evaluation tests and516 corpus fixtures.\n- The AC22 admission regression fails before the repair and passes afterward; no paid session ran.\n- The original dirty E04 checkout is preserved.\n- [Current integration validation](https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-06-i10-e04-review-handoff/validation.md).\n\n## References\n\n- **R1.** [#621](https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/pull/621) — scenario compile declarations, run checks and sub-agent traces (W01–W04).\n- **R2.** [#626](https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/pull/626) — the bootstrapped skill line, conditional and nested deferral, and preset-matched deferral (W05 to W07).\n- **R3.** [#628](https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/pull/628) — conditional composition, footnote and arrow labels, and self-composition (W08, W09).\n- **R4.** [#634](https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/pull/634) — deferred dispatch, dispatch three hops deep, and a sub-agent's first `pf` run (W10 to W12).\n- **R5.** [#638](https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/pull/638) — Claude shell access and nested sub-agent command evidence (W18).\n- **R6.** [#640](https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/pull/640) — the triage rubric's rows for the run classes (W17).\n- **R7.** [#651](https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/pull/651) — the edge workflows composing with `↳` and the corpus test reading the guide's bundles (W19).\n\n- **R8.** [Composition Measurements #661](https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/issues/661) — the shakedown (former W16), live run (former W14) and results publication (former W15), held by I14.\n\n- **R9.** [Architecture Overview](https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-06-622-composition-following-review/architecture-overview.md) — measured structure, flows and reading order.\n- **R10.** [Agent Review](https://github.com/m2ux/prosiform/blob/engineering/artifacts/planning/2026-11-06-i10-e04-review-handoff/agent-reviews.json) — exact-head review, fixed findings and acceptance evidence.\n","labels":[{"id":12732149645,"node_id":"LA_kwDOVNSvEM8AAAAC9uUvjQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/m2ux/prosiform/labels/bot:ai-assisted","name":"bot:ai-assisted","description":"AI assistance disclosure","color":"ededed","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-03T09:03:16Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T12:34:23Z","closed_at":"2026-11-06T12:34:23Z","merged_at":"2026-11-06T12:34:23Z","merge_commit_sha":"d8265c82e797355a55cf7ec7d921949b4d7eb6c0","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"m2ux:i10/e04/main","ref":"i10/e04/main","repo":{"id":1423224592,"node_id":"R_kgDOVNSvEA","name":"prosiform","full_name":"m2ux/prosiform","owner":{"login":"m2ux","id":176900785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCotKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176900785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux","html_url":"https://github.com/m2ux","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m2ux/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"A deterministic compiler for instruction sets written as linked Markdown. Give it a document or a section; it returns that content and every local Markdown dependency it reaches, as one validated bundle.","homepage":"","language":"Python",